Note it prefilters candidates by `findByTelephone` — if you change the key to drop telephone (soundex-based v2), this prefilter must change too or it will miss collisions.

**Exceptions:**
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/DuplicateOwnerException.java` (RuntimeException, message uses identityKey)
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/HouseholdDuplicateException.java`

**409 mapping:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`
- `handleDuplicateOwnerException` — lines 124-134 → `HttpStatus.CONFLICT`
- `handleHouseholdDuplicateException` — lines 145-155 → `HttpStatus.CONFLICT`
- (Also `handleCityCapacityExceededException` lines 165-175 → 409; `DisposableEmailDomainException` → 400 lines 205-215; `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` → 429.)

**Controller entry:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` `addOwner` lines 118-135 (reads `sharesHousehold` flag, calls `createOwner`). Route base `/api` is on `OwnerRestControllerV2` (`@RequestMapping("/api")`), endpoint `POST /api/owners`.

---

## 4. soundex usage

**None in production code.** Only referenced in the test spec comment: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` lines 9-11. No soundex utility class exists in `util/`. You must implement it for the v2 identity key.

---

## 5. Related normalization / matching / soft-delete logic

- **normalizedTelephone (E.164):** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/TelephoneNormalizer.java`, `toE164(String)` lines 55-75 (default country `+61`, strips separators, drops leading `0`, 8-15 digits). Applied in `OwnerMapper` line 63-64 and controller `updateOwner` line 152.
- **lowerEmail:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/EmailNormalizer.java`, `normalize(String)` lines 36-41 (`toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT)`). Applied in `OwnerMapper` line 65-66.
- **email-domain blocklist:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/DisposableEmailDomains.java`, `isDisposable(String)` lines 41-51; blocked set line 28-29 (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Enforced in `ClinicServiceImpl.createOwner` lines 269-271 → `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).
- **soft-match / possibleDuplicate:** `ClinicServiceImpl.flagPossibleDuplicate(Owner, List<Owner>, boolean)` lines 346-353 — flags an owner as a soft duplicate of the lowest-id household member with a *different* telephone; sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`. Never flags when `sharesHousehold`.
- **postcode matching:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/PostcodePolicy.java` — `isValidForCity` lines 47-53, `regionForPostcode` lines 62-77 (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099). Postcode is also a household-key component (HouseholdIdGenerator).
- **deleted / soft-delete flag:** `Owner.deleted` field — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../model/Owner.java` lines 96-97 (`@Column(name="deleted", nullable=false)`, default `false`), getter/setter lines 246-252. Set by `ClinicServiceImpl.deleteOwner` lines 156-159 (`owner.setDeleted(true); ownerRepository.save(owner)`). Honored by `isActive(Owner)` lines 318-320, used to exclude soft-deleted owners from both identity and household duplicate checks (lines 307, 382). Controller `deleteOwner` lines 162-169.

---

## 6. SHA-256 hashing utility

**File:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Sha256.java`
**Method:** `hex(String)` — lines 38-49: returns 64-char **lowercase** hex digest of UTF-8 bytes.
```java
public static String hex(String value) {
    try {
        byte[] digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256").digest(value.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(digest.length * 2);
        for (byte b : digest) {
            sb.append(String.format("%02x", b));
        }
        return sb.toString();
    } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
        throw new IllegalStateException("SHA-256 is required but unavailable", e);
    }
}
```
Currently used only by `HouseholdIdGenerator`. This is the helper to reuse for the v2 identityKey (the test's own `sha256hex` in `AcceptanceBase` lines 282-294 is byte-for-byte identical).

---

## Relevant test files

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — the only tests for identity key + duplicate detection: `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` (lines 14-19, expects 64-hex) and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` (lines 21-28, expects 409 on identical telephone/email/lastName). Spec comment lines 9-11 defines the v2 algorithm (soundex-based).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — black-box harness. Relevant helpers: `sha256hex`/`shaHex` (lines 282-299), `deleteOwner` soft-delete helper (lines 194-197), `structuredOwner`/`withPostcode` payloads (lines 129-142), unique generators.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` — audit support (not duplicate-specific).

There are **no** dedicated unit tests for `OwnerIdentityKey`, `HouseholdIdGenerator`, or `flagPossibleDuplicate` (soft-match) — coverage is only the two black-box acceptance tests above.

